course: dictionary
lesson: 8996
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word skate is a good example. «At skate parks one rider goes in the bowl at a time» means riding on wheels, because skate parks are for skateboards and roller skates.
explain: Ask yourself what would fit. «A skate is also a flat sea fish» only makes sense if you think of the sea, so the words around it give you the clue. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
explain: Some words also change their form. Skate can be a verb, as in «to skate» or «taught him to skate», or a noun, as in «a pair of skates». Look at the words before and after the word to see how it is being used.
fact: Skate can mean to glide on ice with ice skates, or on the ground with roller skates or a skateboard.
fact: A skate is a boot with a blade or wheels on the bottom.
fact: A skate is also a flat sea fish, a bit like a ray.
fact: «A mermaid's purse» is the egg case of a catshark, skate or ray; its curly tendrils hold it to seaweed while the baby grows.
fact: «A helmet greatly lowers the chance of a serious head injury when cycling, skating or scootering.»
exercise: «When the cast came off he told his best mate, who laughed for ages and then taught him to skate for real.» What does skate mean here? | To swim quickly in the sea | To fall over and hit your head | *To glide on ice or on wheels | To cook a fish
exercise: «A mermaid's purse is the egg case of a catshark, skate or ray.» In this sentence, what is a skate? | A park for riding on wheels | A type of cloud | *A flat sea fish, a bit like a ray | A boot with a blade on the bottom
exercise: «Jess put on her new pair of skates before going to the rink.» What is a skate in this sentence? | *A boot with a blade or wheels on the bottom | A helmet with straps | A flat sea fish | To glide across the ice
test: «At skate parks one rider goes in the bowl at a time, and you look before you drop in.» What does skate park mean? | A school hall for sports | A frozen lake for ice skating | *A place where people ride skateboards and roller skates | A place to buy fish from the sea
test: «A helmet greatly lowers the chance of a serious head injury when cycling, skating or scootering.» Why does this sentence matter? | It keeps your feet warm on the ice | *It lowers the chance of a serious head injury | It makes you go faster | It shows that helmets look cool
exam: Tom says that in «A mermaid's purse is the egg case of a catshark, skate or ray», a skate is a skateboard. Is he right? | Yes, because skate always means a skateboard | Yes, because a catshark has wheels | No, because a skate is a boot with a blade | *No, here a skate is a flat sea fish, a bit like a ray
